.\" DECtape(1) manual page
.TH DECtape 1 "May 2026" "waffle8" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
DECtape \- inspect and edit OS/8 DECtape images (.tu56)
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools/DECtape
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B DECtape
is a Python utility for working with OS/8 DECtape images stored in SIMH .tu56
format. It can dump raw 129\-word frames, view OS/8 logical blocks (256 words
over two frames), walk directory segments, add host files, and print file
contents. Directory walking follows DLINKs until the chain ends or loops.
.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B read
.RI "DECtape read " image " " block " [\-\-logical] [\-\-sixbit]"
Dump a DECtape block. By default
.I block
is a physical 129\-word frame; use
.B \-\-logical
to read an OS/8 logical block spanning two frames. With
.B \-\-sixbit
the output is rendered as SIXBIT pairs instead of octal words.
.TP
.B dir
.RI "DECtape dir " image " [" \-b " block ]"
Parse and print an OS/8 directory segment. Defaults to block 1. The utility
prints the header (entry count, origin, DLINK) and each entry’s status,
start block, length in blocks, and raw date.
.TP
.B add
.RI "DECtape add " image " " filename " [" \-n " os8name ]"
Insert a host file into an OS/8 DECtape image (file must end with
.BR .tu56 ).
OS/8 names are uppercased and truncated to 6.2 characters. The image
directory is updated to point at newly written blocks; remaining free space
in the reused entry is split out when possible. Fails if the image or source
file is missing or there is not enough free space.
.TP
.B cat
.RI "DECtape cat " image " " os8file " [" \-a | \-\-ascii ]"
Print file contents from the OS/8 image. The argument may be
.I NAME.EXT
or just
.IR NAME ;
when no extension is given the first name\-only match is used. With
.B \-\-ascii
the high bit of each byte is stripped (useful for ASCII\-8 text).
.TP
.B zero
.RI "DECtape zero " image " [" \-b " blocks ] [" \-o " origin ] [" \-f ]"
Create a blank OS/8 DECtape image filled with zeros and an empty directory at
logical block 1. Defaults: 575 logical blocks (1150 physical frames) and
origin block 070 (first data block). Refuses to overwrite existing files
unless
.B \-f
is given.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Dump logical block 20 as SIXBIT pairs:
.EX
tools/DECtape read \-\-logical \-\-sixbit media/boot-tc08.tu56 20
.EE
.TP
List the directory chain starting at block 1:
.EX
tools/DECtape dir magtape/tc08-unit1.tu56
.EE
.TP
Add a host text file under an explicit OS/8 name:
.EX
tools/DECtape add magtape/work.tu56 docs/note.txt \-n NOTE.TX
.EE
.TP
Print a file as 7\-bit ASCII:
.EX
tools/DECtape cat \-a magtape/work.tu56 NOTE.TX
.EE
.TP
Create a new writable image with a custom size:
.EX
tools/DECtape zero \-b 300 \-o 070 magtape/scratch.tu56
.EE
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B nonzero
An error occurred (missing file, invalid block number, no free space, or other
argument/IO failure).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B tools/DECtape
Command implementation.
.TP
.B tools/tu56/__init__.py
Library used for frame and directory parsing, SIXBIT handling, and image
creation.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tc08 (1),
.BR webdp8 (1),
.BR 8asm (1)
